[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Relation roles use color while stroke pattern shows direction

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[MECHANISM]
UID: MECH-SDOC-BOARD-RELATION-ROLE-STYLES
TITLE: Relation roles use color while stroke pattern shows direction
DEPTH: implemented
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
The Graph view assigns each payload-derived relation role a deterministic hue
from the alphabetically sorted role vocabulary. Golden-angle hue steps keep
adjacent assignments visually separated. The same role name therefore keeps
one color across source-node-type filter groups, the grouped graph key, and
visible graph edges. Edge paths, labels, and arrowheads inherit that hue, while
filter controls show a role-colored dot without implying direction.

Stroke pattern describes direction relative to the focal work item: direct
outgoing edges are solid, direct incoming edges are dashed, and non-focal
transit edges are dotted and subdued. Routing geometry remains independent of
this encoding. The always-available Key disclosure names the three patterns.
Color is an identity aid rather than normative meaning, and the vocabulary
remains payload-derived.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Added by the WORK-GRAPH-NEIGHBORHOOD-VIEW reference implementation on 2026-09-02.
<<<
